to me  [Music]  being a refugee is also being an  alchemist these are individuals who lost  everything and from nothing  are able to manifest so much  and i think  surviving displacement  should be celebrated  [Music]  my name is meimuna hussain kitan i'm the  founder and executive director of the  tia foundation right now we're at my  restaurant flavors from afar in little  ethiopia  little ethiopia is one of the first  african enclaves in california it's a  strip here in los angeles to me  establishing a restaurant here in little  ethiopia made sense with my journey  because my parents are refugees from  ethiopia they had fled in the 70s and i  was born in a refugee camp in somalia in  1980 it just felt like a full circle  to even have the opportunity to find  this space and to establish a restaurant  on the street  i employ  former asylum seekers and refugees that  were displaced and the reason why that's  personal to me is because i know  firsthand that you want to preserve your  dishes from back home it helps you feel  connected to your homeland  the main mission of flavors from afar is  to help immigrant chefs especially women  and to provide a platform to celebrate  their cuisines  oh i love it i i it's different you can  eat different food you can meet  different people  i feel maimuna has given refugees the  opportunity to experience themselves  with the community just an opportunity  to  be who i am represent my palestinian  cuisine as a refugee with people from  all over the world and this is just a  gift  it's nice to give everyone a platform to  be celebrated to be seen you know our  chefs receive five percent of the gross  sales throughout the month we provide  them headshots we curate their menu we  provide marketing for them so there's a  whole package ready to go so by the end  of the month if they want to continue to  pursue maybe a catering business or  pursue working in another restaurant  they have a portfolio that's been  created  what i hope for for the communities and  the chefs that we work with is that  becoming an entrepreneur is possible  and that they do have talents and gifts  to contribute  and a lot of people  have a desire and need to try their  dishes  for so long i felt invisible  and  there wasn't  spaces that were ever appropriate for me  to talk about my family's refugee  journey  so it's just something that was kind of  in the backdrop but you don't talk about  the experience you don't talk about the  ptsd at home you don't talk about  the struggles and the obstacles  to finally have the chance to talk about  these difficult topics and celebrate  people  after  displacement  and really humanizing their stories  celebrating their cuisines  that really means a lot so  while i do this for others i too get the  chance to  feel seen and celebrated  refugees are very very important part of  our society they have skills they have  feelings they have experiences they have  history they have families  flavors from afar is one of the  structures or one of the platforms that  showed that that proved that and showed  refugees to the world in a more powerful  and more beautiful image but there are  so many layers to that refugee and this  has to be seen  i think people misunderstood like they  come from a different country they're  different  but we're not different we're all the  same after 11 years of ups and downs i  would love to just have a sabbatical to  travel back home to ethiopia to see my  relatives to see my grandma who's in  nairobi  hey everyone today i'm about to give a  huge surprise to meimuna founder and  owner of flavors from afar a restaurant  that employs refugee chefs from all  around the world  [Music]  so what's the tia foundation  tia means my love in my family's  language we're refugees from ethiopia  and  our non-profit  was established to help  newly arrived  refugees and immigrants that are  starting over here in the u.s  and how did the restaurant branch from  the non-profit the restaurant was  inspired by survival  i hit a point where i had to think about  sustainability the best way to do that  is by using the resources  that  are around you already we're already  surrounded by talented people who have  food from all over the world  so i launched as a catering service  originally it just you know  took off from there i want to thank you  so much for sharing your story and your  experience with us  and since you do so much for your  community we actually want to give you  something  zell is going to send you 3 000  to continue the amazing work you're  doing  and thanks to  it will be in your bank account in  minutes  so we just we want to thank you so much  come here  you're incredible  [Music]

